From 308c83b3b3d21a07cac79072ab69e0ce8882181f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:52:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Vision: a counter plugin system (lookup, plugin_paths,
 checks, status, close)

A counter was a 'module:Class' that had to be importable already, usually with
PYTHONPATH set by hand. It could not describe itself or its options, nor report status.
If it failed to load, its hub thread died silently and /control showed 'never connected'.

vision/counters/__init__.py, plugin API 1:
- lookup: built-ins, then the 'watchtower.counters' entry points of installed packages
  (pip install a plugin, then counter: its-name), then a plugins: alias, then
  'module:Class'. plugin_paths: in vision.yaml adds folders to the path, relative to that
  file; a folder whose pyproject.toml registers entry points gets the short names without
  being installed. Built-in names cannot be taken over.
- describe/check: optional PLUGIN_API, NAME, DESCRIPTION, NEEDS and OPTIONS on the class.
  A plugin built for a newer API is refused. A key that looks like a misspelt option
  ('confidence' for 'conf') is warned at startup; other keys are left alone, since
  defaults: is shared by every counter.
- run_vision.py --list-counters prints every counter with its description, needs and
  options, and survives one that cannot load.
- The runner merges a plugin's status() (detail / warning / error) into each second's
  report, calls close() on stop, and puts a load failure on /control and the console.
  rescore.py uses the same lookup.
- zone, linecross and mock declare their options. Older plugins with none of the new
  attributes run unchanged.

Checked: 11 new tests, no cv2 needed (37 pass). End to end against this server, with
YOLOv26-FRC-Model's tbavid-colour / tbavid-combo loaded by short name both
pip-installed and via plugin_paths only, without PYTHONPATH:
- 'ball_aera' was flagged as 'ball_area';
- /control showed 'colour 123', and for the combo on a CPU-only machine 'colour 29
  (model off)' with its amber warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
